The graph below shows a quantity modelled by $Q=P+Ae^{kt}$, with the line $Q=50$ dashed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$t$}, ylabel={$Q$},
            xmin=-0.6, xmax=10.6, ymin=-7, ymax=62, samples=100, clip=false,
            ytick={15,50}, xtick={2,4,6,8,10}]
\addplot[dashed, domain=0:10.6] (x, 50);
\addplot[smooth, thick, ->, domain=0:10] {50 - 35*exp(-0.4*x)};
\node[above right] at (axis cs:0.6,50) {$Q=50$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What are the signs of $A$ and $k$?
